@parameters

== Main ==

Run controls, Check Setup and the reports of the last export and run.
__Show Expert Controls__ shows the advanced solver settings (they keep
their values, and are exported, while hidden).

== Geometry ==

Meshes (simulated bodies and rigid obstacles), their transforms,
subdomains, materials, sidesets with boundary conditions, and initial
conditions.

== Time ==

Quasistatic or dynamic, the time range and step, and the time integrator.

== Contact ==

Contact on/off, the contact distance __dhat__, friction, adhesion and
collision detection.

== Solver ==

Linear and nonlinear solvers, line search and stopping criteria. Newton is
the method that converges on contact scenes.

== Output ==

What PolyFEM writes: the log, result fields (VTK-HDF by default; body ids
and contact forces are on by default), and optional files.

== Global ==

The body load (gravity: see above) and optional units.

== Remeshing ==

Adaptive remeshing during the run (rarely needed).
